  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a7df911688ca425f8f129e9c77e6df6e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Readable
  Title: Acquisitions ledger, 1803 - present
  Body: 'Lot 1. Thralls, gallery stock. Live. Kept sedated on laudanum and lamb''s
    blood. Restock as required.


    Lot 5. The founder. CONTAINED. On no account
    to be opened, fed or spoken to.


    Lot 9. Portrait of the Countess Morvayne.
    Live. Feed monthly. Keep the frame locked.


    Lot 14. Valley stock, eleven,
    received this spring. Live. Transferred to gallery stock.


    Beneath the last
    entry, in the curator''s hand: "Every piece is authentic. I never once lied to
    them."'
  ReadClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d827ef23d1b788f4b92b1131a21aa803, type: 3}
  Verb: Read ledger
